[b]Slower battles, where timing, rest and defence decide the fight — and heroes matter.[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Fights last longer.[/b] Every man tires: a spent soldier attacks once where a fresh one attacks five times.
[*][b]Timing matters.[/b] When you commit a formation counts as much as which troops you bring.
[*][b]Rest your troops.[/b] A rested line beats a spent one. Hold a fresh reserve, then throw shock infantry or cavalry at a line that has been fighting for two minutes.
[*][b]Your orders set how hard they fight.[/b] Holding men save their strength; charging men spend it all.
[*][b]Heroes carry the fight.[/b] They tire slowest, and late in a battle they are often the freshest men on the field.
[/list]

[h1]How it works, at a glance[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]An Athletics bar[/b] for every fighter — his stamina, as big as his Athletics skill.
[*][b]Attacks, kicks and blocks drain it;[/b] rest refills it in about a minute. Clean blocks and parries let it refill while you defend.
[*][b]Tired men fight worse:[/b] a pause between attacks once their stored swings run out (save a few up and strike them back to back; no slow motion), a slower run, weaker lucky hits, and tired AI start guessing which way to block.
[*][b]Tired AI act on your orders:[/b] below a floor set by the order (hold 60%, advance 40%, charge 20%) they stop swinging and defend, shield up, until they catch their breath. Order the charge and they surge again.
[*][b]Sprint:[/b] hold Left Ctrl for a short burst of speed paid from your stamina; AI formations sprint on a new charge.
[*][b]See it:[/b] your bar under your health; in the orders menu and when you hold ALT, every formation's stamina and how many men are [i]ready[/i] — yours and the enemy's.
[/list]

Every number, with tables: [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/trax_combat_enhancements/blob/main/docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md]How it works — the player guide[/url].

[h1]Good to know[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Not an overhaul.[/b] Vanilla troops, weapons and AI. Nothing in your save: add or remove it mid-campaign.
[*]Every number is a setting, live even mid-battle — in [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2859238197]MCM[/url] ([b]optional[/b]) or a commented config file. A master switch turns it all off mid-battle, to compare.
[*]Game v1.4.8, singleplayer. No requirements, no Harmony. Works beside RTS Camera and War Sails.
[*][b]Not with Realistic Battle Mod (RBM)[/b] — the deep, much-loved overhaul with its own stamina. This is the light road on vanilla's troops; use one or the other.
[/list]

Bugs, balance, a mod it fights with: tell me in the comments or on [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/trax_combat_enhancements/issues]GitHub[/url]. Attaching [i]trax_combat.log[/i] (beside the config file) helps a lot.

Made by two of us: the code by Claude (Opus 5.5), an AI; the idea and playtesting by [url=https://github.com/TraxData313]Trax[/url], Bible believer and engineer in AI/ML/Python/Applied Maths.

Free and open — public domain. Source: [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/trax_combat_enhancements]github.com/TraxData313/trax_combat_enhancements[/url]
